# cafe-llama.cpp integration proposal for ODS (English summary)

**Project:** ODS  
**Date:** 2026-10-06  
**Status:** Architecture summary mirrored into ODS fork  
**Upstream:** https://github.com/quimmedes/cafe-llama.cpp  
**ODS scaffold:** `ods/docs/CAFE-LLAMA.md`, `ods/services/cafe-llama/`

## Executive summary

cafe-llama.cpp is a llama.cpp fork focused on real capacity for large MoE models and long contexts on modest hardware. Key additions:

- First-class MoE offload to pinned host RAM (`-hmoe`), system RAM (`-cmoe`) or SSD streaming (`-ssd`)
- Turbo low-bit KV cache (turbo4/3/2) with mandatory flash-attention
- Qwen 3.8 Flash Next PLE / N-gram table controls
- Strong MTP speculative decoding (`--spec-type draft-mtp`, recommended `--spec-draft-n-max 4`)
- Native safetensors loading (no intermediate GGUF)
- Linux x64 prebuilt binaries are available; other build targets require a compatible release archive and are not enabled by the ODS activation hook.

**Role in ODS:** optional advanced runtime that remains API- and GGUF-compatible with the existing `llama-server`. It expands the configuration space that Inference Configuration Discovery (ICD) can explore; it does not replace the baseline runtime.

## Integration shape

```text
ods/services/cafe-llama/
├── manifest.yaml
├── entrypoint.sh
└── README.md
```

Expose priority flags in Dashboard advanced settings and `LLAMA_ARG_*` / Model Switchboard:

- `-ngl`, `-hmoe`/`-nhmoe`, `-cmoe`/`-ncmoe`, `-ssd`/`-nssd`
- `-c`, `-ctk`/`-ctv` (incl. turbo*), `-fa`
- `--spec-type`, `--spec-draft-n-max`, `-md`
- `--no-ngram` / `--ngram-ssd`
- batch / threads / parallel

Activation: explicit `CAFE_LLAMA_ENABLED=true` plus a model activation request, after the curated service recipe is installed. The host agent currently supports host-native Linux NVIDIA or explicitly configured CPU builds; the standard `llama-server` remains the default.

## Evidence rules

Only **MEASURED** results on target hardware may be used to claim local performance. Upstream numbers and community posts are **REPORTED** or **OBSERVED**.

## Relation to other runtimes

| Runtime | Role |
|---------|------|
| llama-server | Baseline, wide compatibility |
| **cafe-llama.cpp** | Advanced MoE / Turbo KV / MTP drop-in |
| TensorFold | Family-specific kernels + exact speculative |
| Strata / heterogeneous | >VRAM placement |
| Bonsai-style kernels | Extreme quant evidence |

